|> 
|> You are experiencing "color flash".  This happens when you use up all of your hardware
|> color table in one application.  You move to out of the window and the color table gets
|> swapped out and replaced to supply the original colors.
|> 
|> You can:
|> - Use fewer different colors (limit is 256 and openwin reserves some colors)
|> - Get hardware that supports multiple hardware color tables (GS or GT cards from Sun)
|> - Live with it
|> 

Hi all, the newest version 1.7 has a -usedefcmap option which will force 
xboingto use the default colourmap. Problem being that if you have a really 
complex pixture on your root window then it may fail. Also, use the 
-pointergrab option in Version 1.6 to force the mouse pointer to be confined
to the arena.

Note that V1.7 will be out soon with quite a few changes and bug fixes :-)

hop that helps
